# Found by this harness (#1349): with double buffering off,
# FrameResourceManager::EndFrame deleted a frame's old fence without forgetting
# the id, and deleted it AGAIN at that slot's next EndFrame. By then the
# backend had reissued the handle to GPUReadbackStats, whose live readback
# fence the second delete destroyed: GL_INVALID_VALUE ("<sync> is not the name
# of a sync object") on every later frame. The fixture fails any render tick
# that leaves a GL error, so replaying this is the regression check.
olo-state-machine-trace 1
seed 0
initial path=forward size=320x180 msaa=1 upscale=off features= blended=0 buffering=2 pose=0
op frames-in-flight 1
op path deferred
op frames-in-flight 2
op frames-in-flight 1
